d><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/watch-iafs-tejas-steals-the-show-at-wings-over-ganges-aerial-display-in-varanasi/articleshow/135187162.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T14:38:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135187567,imgsize-54992.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Vote chori’ protests: Kharge asks Congress MPs to be in Delhi from Oct 30-Nov 1]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/vote-chori-protests-kharge-asks-congress-mps-to-be-in-delhi-from-oct-30-nov-1/articleshow/135187186.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135187186.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/vote-chori-protests-kharge-asks-congress-mps-to-be-in-delhi-from-oct-30-nov-1/articleshow/135187186.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/vote-chori-protests-kharge-asks-congress-mps-to-be-in-delhi-from-oct-30-nov-1/articleshow/135187186.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T14:27:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135187313,imgsize-110584.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Give priority to local artisans’: PM Modi’s festive shopping appeal as Diwali approaches]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/give-priority-to-local-artisans-pm-modis-festive-shopping-appeal-as-diwali-approaches/articleshow/135186794.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135186794.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Prime Minister Narendra Modi urged citizens to support local artisans by prioritizing their products while shopping for festivals. He emphasized that doing so would strengthen the 'Vocal for Local' campaign and promote a self-reliant India. Modi highlighted successful local exports such as makhana and arhar dal to various international markets. Additionally, he discussed efforts aimed at reviving traditional skills and farming practices, including natural cotton cultivation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/give-priority-to-local-artisans-pm-modis-festive-shopping-appeal-as-diwali-approaches/articleshow/135186794.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/give-priority-to-local-artisans-pm-modis-festive-shopping-appeal-as-diwali-approaches/articleshow/135186794.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T14:09:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135186874,imgsize-78812.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Now that Nitish is no longer there': Expelled Anant Singh says has no regrets, to float own party]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jdu-is-finished-bihar-strongman-anant-singh-to-float-own-party-after-expulsion/articleshow/135186680.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135186680.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jdu-is-finished-bihar-strongman-anant-singh-to-float-own-party-after-expulsion/articleshow/135186680.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jdu-is-finished-bihar-strongman-anant-singh-to-float-own-party-after-expulsion/articleshow/135186680.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T14:07:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135186865,imgsize-871491.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Don't be spectator, show leadership': EAM Jaishankar to UN on terrorism, global crises]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-be-spectator-show-leadership-eam-jaishankar-to-un-on-terrorism-global-crises/articleshow/135185782.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135185782.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In his latest statements, external affairs minister S Jaishankar called for a more robust leadership from the UN to confront pressing world issues. He highlighted a significant gap in global decision-making that leaves many regions, particularly in the Global South, behind in critical areas like finance, fuel, food, and fertilizer. Emphasizing the importance of fair AI development, Jaishankar encourages strategies that ensure widespread access to its benefits, fostering international cooperation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-be-spectator-show-leadership-eam-jaishankar-to-un-on-terrorism-global-crises/articleshow/135185782.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-be-spectator-show-leadership-eam-jaishankar-to-un-on-terrorism-global-crises/articleshow/135185782.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T12:53:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135185916,imgsize-91824.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Centre rushes 250 RAF personnel to Arunachal after violent protests over hydropower project]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-rushes-250-raf-personnel-to-arunachal-after-violent-protests-over-hydropower-project/articleshow/135185576.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135185576.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Centre has deployed two Rapid Action Force companies comprising around 250 CRPF personnel to Arunachal Pradesh following violent protests against the proposed 11,200-MW Siang Upper Multipurpose Project. A mob torched an NHPC office and a police station in Pasighat, injuring over 40 police personnel. The project, seen as a strategic counter to China’s mega dam, faces opposition from indigenous tribes fearing displacement and submergence of villages.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-rushes-250-raf-personnel-to-arunachal-after-violent-protests-over-hydropower-project/articleshow/135185576.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-rushes-250-raf-personnel-to-arunachal-after-violent-protests-over-hydropower-project/articleshow/135185576.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T12:41:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135185738,imgsize-997927.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Not less than a pilgrimage’: PM Modi marks 12 years of Mann Ki Baat - top quotes]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/not-less-than-a-pilgrimage-pm-modi-marks-12-years-of-mann-ki-baat-top-quotes/articleshow/135184634.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135184634.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/not-less-than-a-pilgrimage-pm-modi-marks-12-years-of-mann-ki-baat-top-quotes/articleshow/135184634.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/not-less-than-a-pilgrimage-pm-modi-marks-12-years-of-mann-ki-baat-top-quotes/articleshow/135184634.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T11:37:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135185011,imgsize-90338.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Foreign-funded conspiracy to destabilise India’: Telangana BJP chief targets Congress over Jamia graffiti]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/foreign-funded-conspiracy-to-destabilise-india-telangana-bjp-chief-targets-congress-over-jamia-graffiti/articleshow/135183499.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135183499.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/foreign-funded-conspiracy-to-destabilise-india-telangana-bjp-chief-targets-congress-over-jamia-graffiti/articleshow/135183499.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/foreign-funded-conspiracy-to-destabilise-india-telangana-bjp-chief-targets-congress-over-jamia-graffiti/articleshow/135183499.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T10:50:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135183850,imgsize-117016.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Thanks BJP for promoting': Rahul Gandhi takes swipe at Centre over Nov 1 rally at Delhi's Ramlila Maidan]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/thanks-bjp-for-promoting-rahul-gandhi-takes-swipe-at-centre-over-nov-1-rally-at-delhis-ramlila-maidan/articleshow/135183667.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135183667.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[On November 1, Rahul Gandhi is set to lead a rally to rally citizens against alleged vote theft, spotlighting issues like voter list inaccuracies and the response to complainants. The BJP has voiced concerns over the timing due to its proximity to the 1984 anti-Sikh riots memorial. Several organizations, including Delhi's Chamber of Trade and Industry, have expressed disapproval.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/thanks-bjp-for-promoting-rahul-gandhi-takes-swipe-at-centre-over-nov-1-rally-at-delhis-ramlila-maidan/articleshow/135183667.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/thanks-bjp-for-promoting-rahul-gandhi-takes-swipe-at-centre-over-nov-1-rally-at-delhis-ramlila-maidan/articleshow/135183667.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T10:40:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135183763,imgsize-135160.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[PM Modi to inaugurate RBI's Rs 169-crore data centre in Bhubaneswar, second after Navi Mumbai]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-to-inaugurate-rbis-rs-169-crore-data-centre-in-bhubaneswar-second-after-navi-mumbai/articleshow/135183306.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135183306.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Prime Minister Narendra Modi will inaugurate the Reserve Bank of India's data centre and Cybersecurity Training Institute. This inauguration is aimed at strengthening Odisha's digital infrastructure and enhancing financial data security. The data centre in Jatni will be the second of its kind in the country, following Navi Mumbai. Modi's visit includes a helicopter journey to Khurda before reaching the data centre.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-to-inaugurate-rbis-rs-169-crore-data-centre-in-bhubaneswar-second-after-navi-mumbai/articleshow/135183306.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-to-inaugurate-rbis-rs-169-crore-data-centre-in-bhubaneswar-second-after-navi-mumbai/articleshow/135183306.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T10:10:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135183341,imgsize-78812.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Drug trafficking crackdown: Amit Shah hails Operation Trident; Rs 100 crore hawala transactions exposed, 18 arrested]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/drug-trafficking-crackdown-amit-shah-hails-operation-trident-rs-100-crore-hawala-transactions-exposed-18-arrested/articleshow/135182867.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135182867.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Union home minister Amit Shah announced Operation Trident, which targeted an international narcotics cartel in India. The operation, conducted in Assam, Mizoram, and Manipur, uncovered significant hawala transactions and led to arrests. Authorities froze numerous bank accounts and seized illegal items, including detonators and cash. Shah emphasized the government's commitment to eradicating drug networks by December 31, 2029.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/drug-trafficking-crackdown-amit-shah-hails-operation-trident-rs-100-crore-hawala-transactions-exposed-18-arrested/articleshow/135182867.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/drug-trafficking-crackdown-amit-shah-hails-operation-trident-rs-100-crore-hawala-transactions-exposed-18-arrested/articleshow/135182867.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T09:56:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Shivanghi Payal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135183209,imgsize-79488.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Ignore strike calls': LPG distributor body ahead of Rahul Gandhi's rally in Delhi]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ignore-strike-calls-lpg-distributor-body-ahead-of-rahul-gandhis-rally-in-delhi/articleshow/135182318.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135182318.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ignore-strike-calls-lpg-distributor-body-ahead-of-rahul-gandhis-rally-in-delhi/articleshow/135182318.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ignore-strike-calls-lpg-distributor-body-ahead-of-rahul-gandhis-rally-in-delhi/articleshow/135182318.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T08:55:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aastha Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135182490,imgsize-117218.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Prioritise welfare over military directives’: India raps Pak on minority rights at UN]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/prioritise-welfare-over-military-directives-india-raps-pak-on-minority-rights-at-un/articleshow/135180093.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135180093.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Speaking at an interactive dialogue with the Special Rapporteur on Minority Issues at the UN General Assembly's Third Committee, India's First Secretary at the Permanent Mission to the UN, Raghoo Puri, called out Pakistan's conduct and said its representatives should focus on the welfare of their own people instead of taking directions from the military.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/prioritise-welfare-over-military-directives-india-raps-pak-on-minority-rights-at-un/articleshow/135180093.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/prioritise-welfare-over-military-directives-india-raps-pak-on-minority-rights-at-un/articleshow/135180093.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T05:32:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135180216,imgsize-725374.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Suspicious pigeon with coded ring, Pak currency causes a flutter in Jammu]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/suspicious-pigeon-with-coded-ring-pak-currency-causes-a-flutter-in-jammu/articleshow/135176763.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135176763.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[An official pointed out that such episodes are not uncommon in border areas of J&amp;K and Punjab, where pigeons have been used for smuggling or for sending messages across the frontier. On Saturday, the pigeon was found near a temple in Samba’s border area of Mawa around 6.40am and was immediately captured by locals after they spotted a ring tied to its leg.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/suspicious-pigeon-with-coded-ring-pak-currency-causes-a-flutter-in-jammu/articleshow/135176763.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/suspicious-pigeon-with-coded-ring-pak-currency-causes-a-flutter-in-jammu/articleshow/135176763.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T03:39:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sanjay Khajuria</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135176811,imgsize-155804.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rs 10 lakh cover for 45 paise: Counter rail ticket buyers get insurance option]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rs-10-lakh-cover-for-45-paise-counter-rail-ticket-buyers-get-insurance-option/articleshow/135177585.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135177585.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The scheme has provision for payment of Rs 7.5 lakh for permanent partial disability and up to Rs 2 lakh for hospitalisation expenses arising from injuries, as well as Rs 10,000 towards transportation of mortal remains of deceased passengers. The Railway Board has directed all its zones to implement the facility.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rs-10-lakh-cover-for-45-paise-counter-rail-ticket-buyers-get-insurance-option/articleshow/135177585.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rs-10-lakh-cover-for-45-paise-counter-rail-ticket-buyers-get-insurance-option/articleshow/135177585.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T02:14:19+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135177758,imgsize-184456.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[CBI files FIR against IL&amp;FS Energy, top execs in Rs 212cr Canara Bank loan fraud case]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cbi-files-fir-against-ilfs-energy-top-execs-in-rs-212cr-canara-bank-loan-fraud-case/articleshow/135177586.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135177586.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[CBI has named M/s IL&amp;FS Energy Development Company Ltd, its MD and directors — Sunil Wadhwa, Anoop Seth, Hari Sankaran, Ramesh Chandra Bawa and Arun Kumar Saha — and unknown public servants and private individuals as accused. The case was registered on Oct 21 following a complaint by Canara Bank’s circle office in Bandra.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cbi-files-fir-against-ilfs-energy-top-execs-in-rs-212cr-canara-bank-loan-fraud-case/articleshow/135177586.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cbi-files-fir-against-ilfs-energy-top-execs-in-rs-212cr-canara-bank-loan-fraud-case/articleshow/135177586.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T02:07:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Raj Shekhar Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135177742,imgsize-95086.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[ED moves Supreme Court against HC order to quash case against portal, founder]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ed-moves-supreme-court-against-hc-order-to-quash-case-against-portal-founder/articleshow/135177481.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135177481.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The directorate, which filed an appeal almost five months after the HC pronounced the order on May 29, also took the ground that the HC passed the order five months and 26 days after the judgement was reserved and it was in violation of SC’s guidelines that the verdict should be delivered within three months.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ed-moves-supreme-court-against-hc-order-to-quash-case-against-portal-founder/articleshow/135177481.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ed-moves-supreme-court-against-hc-order-to-quash-case-against-portal-founder/articleshow/135177481.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T01:53:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Amit Anand Choudhary</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135177711,imgsize-148868.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Defer Nov 1 rally, will hit festive business, traders urge Rahul; BJP raps Congress]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/defer-nov-1-rally-will-hit-festive-business-traders-urge-rahul-bjp-raps-congress/articleshow/135177587.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135177587.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[CTI chairman Brijesh Goyal said Delhi records Rs 25,000 crore in business on Dhanteras across major sectors. CTI claimed that traders suffered losses of Rs 3,000 crore in Oct due to rallies and road closures in Connaught Place, India Gate and central Delhi. BJP claimed some Congress allies have disagreed with Rahul Gandhi’s decision to hold the rally on Nov 1.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/defer-nov-1-rally-will-hit-festive-business-traders-urge-rahul-bjp-raps-congress/articleshow/135177587.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/defer-nov-1-rally-will-hit-festive-business-traders-urge-rahul-bjp-raps-congress/articleshow/135177587.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T01:49:42+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135177705,imgsize-57824.cms"/></item></channel></rss>